    inventory.put(title, inventory.get(title) + quantity);
} else {
    inventory.put(title, quantity);
}
```
In C++, `inventory[title]` returns a reference to the value. If `title` is not in the map, it inserts it with a value-initialized int (which is 0). Then `+= quantity` adds `quantity` to it. So 0 + quantity = quantity. This perfectly matches the Java behavior.

For `removeBook`:
Java:
```java
