`uNum` = 4294967291 (0xFFFFFFFB)
4294967291 % 8 = 3
4294967291 / 8 = 536870911
536870911 % 8 = 7
536870911 / 8 = 67108863
67108863 % 8 = 7
67108863 / 8 = 8388607
8388607 % 8 = 7
8388607 / 8 = 1048575
1048575 % 8 = 7
1048575 / 8 = 131071
131071 % 8 = 7
131071 / 8 = 16383
16383 % 8 = 7
16383 / 8 = 2047
2047 % 8 = 7
2047 / 8 = 255
255 % 8 = 7
255 / 8 = 31
31 % 8 = 7
31 / 8 = 3
3 % 8 = 3
3 / 8 = 0
Result: "37777777773"
Java's `Integer.toOctalString(-5)` is "37777777773". Matches!

