In C++, we can use the SQLite3 C API directly, or a wrapper. Since the standard library doesn't have an SQLite wrapper, I'll use the C API (`sqlite3.h`). I should include the necessary headers and manage the database connection using RAII (Resource Acquisition Is Initialization) to ensure the connection is closed properly.

